# status-digest.env.example — configuration for status-digest.sh.
#
# Copy to $HOME/.config/run-issues/digest.env (or point
# RUN_ISSUES_DIGEST_ENV_FILE somewhere else) and edit. Nothing here is required:
# with no file at all the digest keeps its built-in defaults and, lacking a
# recipient or `gws`, simply prints the body to stdout.
#
# The file is sourced FIRST, so a value here is a default that a command-line
# flag (--to, --max-silence, --min-class) still overrides.
#
# NO SECRETS HERE. `gws` carries its own Google credentials; this file holds only
# a recipient address and a few thresholds. Keep tokens out of it, like the
# poller.env sibling.

# Recipient(s) for the digest email, comma-separated. Overridden by --to. Unset
# (and no --to), the body is printed to stdout instead of mailed — the package
# stays usable without Google Workspace, and you can pipe it anywhere.
RUN_ISSUES_DIGEST_TO="you@example.com"

# Days of silence after which the digest is sent even when the situation is
# unchanged, so a long quiet spell never reads as "the digest is broken". An
# unchanged situation within this window sends nothing. Overridden by
# --max-silence; 0 disables the heartbeat entirely. Default 7.
#RUN_ISSUES_DIGEST_MAX_SILENCE=7

# Lowest class to include: attention (only runs needing a human) or stalled
# (attention + wedged/orphaned runs). Overridden by --min-class. Default stalled.
#RUN_ISSUES_DIGEST_MIN_CLASS=stalled

# Rows shown per class_reason group before the list is capped with "…ja M muuta".
# Default 10.
#RUN_ISSUES_DIGEST_MAX_ROWS=10

# Subject line prefix. Default "run-issues -kooste".
#RUN_ISSUES_DIGEST_SUBJECT_PREFIX="run-issues -kooste"

# The gws command. Default "gws". Mainly a test injection point; leave unset.
#RUN_ISSUES_DIGEST_GWS=gws

# Fingerprint state file. Default
# ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/run-issues/last-digest.sha. The digest
# stores the last-sent fingerprint (line 1) and send epoch (line 2) here so an
# unchanged situation stays quiet. Override only for tests.
#RUN_ISSUES_DIGEST_STATE_FILE="$HOME/.local/state/run-issues/last-digest.sha"
